From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:07:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 128/138] media: apple: t7000 ISP: trace=1 hang hunting, never
 gate ps_isp with transactions outstanding

trace=1 prints every ISP-window, PMGR, pin and ref clock write before
it happens and sleeps 50 ms (task context), trace=2 adds the reads;
markers for open/ioctl/release, every IO command, H2T posts, T2H
messages, teardown steps and boot stages. With the console on tty0 the
last line names the access that hung. Writable at runtime.

The SoC hung on the first stream run (open -> re-boot -> START -> frame
-> close). New hazard on that path: tearing down an ISP whose pipeline
was streaming. If the TLIMIT drains (+0x44/+0x68) still read non-zero
after 100 ms + another 1 s, the CPU stop now sets drain_failed and the
teardown leaves ps_isp/ps_media ON (memory leaked on purpose) instead of
power-gating a block with outstanding transactions; later boots refuse.

stream_nostart=1: START configures the channel but posts no buffers
and sends no CH_START (no frame DMA), to split the path.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
